<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31643" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">objectĭo</span></b> , ōnis,
			f.
		obicio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a throwing</i> or <i>putting
			before</i> (post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prorae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ambros. Ep. 100, § 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saxorum objectione tutari,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 6, 191</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>an upbraiding,
				reproach</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">objectio nominis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. ad Uxor. 2, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">objectionem repellere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ambros. Ep. 84</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ejus facti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 5, § 445</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>An objection</i>, <i><span class="en">Ambros.
				Fide, 4, 9, 100</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Aug.
				Ep. 166, 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Macr. Somn. Scip. 2,
				16, 20</span></i>; Aug. Nat. et <i><span class="en">Grat.
			10</span></i>; Schol. <i><span class="en">Juv. 10, 324</span></i> and
			346.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b> As
			rhet. fig., = anthypophora, Jul. Rufin. Schem. Dian. §
		4.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
